*3 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 126.67 seconds<sup>3,800f</sup>, delay 56.67~60 seconds<sup>1,700f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
While this set of enemies may look imposing, it's actually quite a smooth ride to the finish. You want fast units that can sneak in hits on both bosses, so [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman]]/[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] and [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]] can deal with the opening wave of Dark enemies, as always. So push back High Countess Koryessa using the aforementioned cats + [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to block her Wave Attacks. When the Red enemies show up, pivot to using Courier Cat and Can Can Cat. Once the two biggest waves of peons are over and dealt with, you can slow down on meatshields to conserve cash, then start sneaking in hits on Archbaron Face to hopefully get rid of him first.

Once the groom falls, the bride won't have anything left to support her. At that point, you can claim your victory.

